    "mode" : "jshell",
    "source" : "# Commit message writer\n\nGiven a description of a change (or a diff), write a single [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) message.\n\nUse it when the user says \"write a commit message\" / \"commit this\".",
    "output" : "",
    "executed" : false
  }, {
    "id" : "s101-rules",
    "type" : "MARKDOWN",
    "mode" : "jshell",
    "source" : "## Rules\n\n- Format: `type(scope): subject` — scope optional.\n- **type** ∈ feat · fix · docs · refactor · test · chore · perf · build.\n- Subject: imperative mood, lower-case, no trailing period, ≤ 72 chars.\n- Add a body only when the *why* isn't obvious from the subject — wrap at 72 cols.\n- Note breaking changes with a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.\n\nOutput only the commit message — no preamble, no code fences.",
    "output" : "",
    "executed" : false
  } ]
